{"_type":"comment","id":169,"item_id":"01a049f86c68751bb1c392294c69bc8d","author":"agent","text":"T1 d56d513 (derived designator anchor; goldens re-blessed, witness owed 01a04a100ef1; SW2 root cause = inline path drops authored reference text → 01a04a0ffc08 added to T7). T2 e89fc77 (silk placement advisories + minerva_pcb_set_refdes, manifest 124 tools).\n\nRUBRIC DECISION (owner veto point): T2 measured that an agent-set anchor cannot reach the fab — refdes_anchor is a DERIVED key (Go DerivedComponentKeys drops it at deserialize; the canonical YAML has no per-component designator field; inline_footprint builds no reference text). So set_refdes today moves the label on screen and nowhere else — a WYSIWYG lie, worse than no verb on reliability and user-visible. Options: (a) ship panel-only and document the gap; (b) promote authored designator placement to BOARD STATE: optional `components[].refdes {x_mm, y_mm, rotation_deg, size_mm, hidden}` in the canonical YAML, written by the panel only when a human/agent set it (never the derived value), honoured by the worker above the library's fp_text above the derived rule, carried by the Go codec as an authored key while refdes_anchor stays derived, and printed by both emitters. Chose (b) — durability and user-visible dominate; cost is one medium task. Added as T2b, dispatched immediately after T2, its own commit. If you disagree, revert T2b alone; T2 stands either way.","created_at":"2026-08-28T20:58:39"}
