{"_type":"comment","id":171,"item_id":"01a049f86c68751bb1c392294c69bc8d","author":"agent","text":"Fold 1 e119b1d: A1 (suggestion verb-shaped, suggested_slot on the row; Go/manifest descriptions byte-equal), A2 (kicad bottom reference text mirrored, rotation negated per PlacementTransform.angle), B1 (validate returns `placement` = sent keys only; set_refdes_anchor overlays it; verb writes whenever a key was sent, `changed` = what moved) + notes B2/B3/B4/B5/C2/C3/A(c)/typing/scrub. Cold re-review: approve_with_notes — all three resolutions proven at the line, no new defect, pin test_part_geometry_contracts 71 verified; note: ANCHOR_KEYS mirrored by hand in Python and a GD literal (two mirrors, acceptable). Codex batched review launched on 864a99c..e119b1d (goldens excluded).","created_at":"2026-08-28T23:36:50"}
{"_type":"comment","id":172,"item_id":"01a049f86c68751bb1c392294c69bc8d","author":"agent","text":"Codex batched review (864a99c..e119b1d): must_fix ×5 + note. Dispositions: REJECTED #1 \"silk_over_silk only examines designator pairs\" — that is the goal as written (designator crossing another designator/outline/board silk); two footprints' authored silk overlapping is a footprint-library defect, not a placement one; REJECTED \"view_state docs outside goals\" — approved remora; REJECTED \"comments not salient\" — no line cited, the re-reviewer's grep found none. ACCEPTED → fold 2: #2 occupied extent must include stroke half-width and arc sweep extrema; #3 kicad loose path must negate a bottom pad's local rotation (PlacementTransform.angle); #4 set_refdes bounds must include the stroke; #5 hover card must clip to a canvas smaller than the card; #6 unused refdes_anchor import in gerber.py. Codex re-checks the fold after.","created_at":"2026-08-28T23:40:25"}
