{"_type":"comment","id":177,"item_id":"01a049f86c68751bb1c392294c69bc8d","author":"agent","text":"DEFERRED FULL SUITE run 2026-08-29 00:22–00:5x PT on 01777cc (Minerva down): pytest 2865 passed / 3 failed / 4 skipped / 3 xfailed (5:09); GD: 379 suites PASS, 2 FAIL (test_export_yaml_verb 31/3, test_trace_pour_terminator 10/1), 8268 assertions passed. Reds: test_gc9_silk_dfm ×2 (hand-listed GC9_TYPES stale after the new advisory types — the scoped set missed this direct consumer), test_candidate_overlay (baseline carries 8 gc9_silk_under_part rows the candidate does not), test_trace_pour_terminator §5 (NPTH-bridged net link no longer drawn — suspect T3 bare-island rule), test_export_yaml_verb 4a–c (standing \"no fabricable geometry\" lead prefixed to status text — attribution pending). Fix loop dispatched; result will be appended and pushed.","created_at":"2026-08-29T00:33:53"}
{"_type":"comment","id":178,"item_id":"01a049f86c68751bb1c392294c69bc8d","author":"agent","text":"Full-suite round 1 = a9948ff (+ f0084d9 pin note). Attribution: test_gc9_silk_dfm ×2 IN-BATCH (hand-listed GC9 family; now derived from GC9_ADVISORY_TYPES + _COUNT_KEYS); test_candidate_overlay — the failure is in-batch but the hole is PRE-EXISTING: ir_candidates.check_candidates dropped every advisory row (partitioned findings only); an overlay adds traces/vias only so silk advisories can never name candidate geometry → now reported as baseline.advisories + baseline_counts (reply-shape ADDITION; 230 consumer tests green; docs/drc.md); test_trace_pour_terminator §5 PRE-EXISTING since 579f8ab (TC8): fixture authored a bottom part's land on B.Cu, but pads[].layers are footprint-local and flip on placement — F.Cu is the intent (proved at base with a git-archive harness, scratchpad/tc9basefull); test_export_yaml_verb 4a–c PRE-EXISTING since 754dda9 (TC8): status text carries the standing board-condition lead; suite now strips _status_lead() like its siblings, and is pinned at 34 (first trustworthy run). Consumer re-run on f0084d9: pytest 78/78, GD 11/11 (7 real-worker suites real_worker_used=true). Full-suite status: pytest 2865 pass + these 3 fixed; GD 379 pass + these 2 fixed = the deferred suite is green for range 864a99c..f0084d9 as of 2026-08-29 00:5x PT (the two GD suites and three pytest files were re-executed individually rather than the whole suite a second time). Pushed.","created_at":"2026-08-29T00:47:35"}
{"_type":"comment","id":180,"item_id":"01a04b85e62079198f6366db6b0d1acd","author":"agent","text":"Landed d999969 on minerva-plugins main (Mac). hover_card pref (pcb_prefs registry, default on) → Options ▸ View ▸ Show hover card; read_state/apply carry it under a new `view` block (accepted_keys, manifest + tools.md updated). GAP_PX 14→19. Canvas: _hover_card_enabled() gates _update_hover_card; _pin_hover_card_for_pad pins the clicked pad's card in INSPECT_PIN while off (_hover_card_pinned; cleared by clear_hover_card, released to hover when the toggle returns). test_pcb_hover_card §6 = 14 checks, EXPECTED_SUITES 67→81, snap_prefs_fixture covers the key. gd-syntax-check passed on all 6 files. GD SUITE NOT RUN — Godot editor open on the Mac; owner re-HITLs next, run test_pcb_hover_card + test_pcb_pin_inspector then.","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:21:32"}
{"_type":"comment","id":181,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Landed 647717d on minerva-plugins main (Mac). PCBPanel.gd 7468→6420; pcb_pin_selection_section.gd deleted; canvas 'Set trace width…' menu + reveal flow removed; zone/via cards + Group line in pcb_hover_card.gd; Pin Select click pins the pad card regardless of the toggle. Six suites re-pinned (see commit) — AUTHORED, NOT RUN (Godot editor open). Review notes: zone hover fixture moved to the top layer so the pick does not depend on the default layer view; via_lines builds the copper index once per hovered via (heaviest card). Owner re-HITL next; then run hover_card, pin_inspector, panel_layout, panel_ui, canvas_input_probe, via_edit_and_fab_stage.","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:53:34"}
{"_type":"comment","id":183,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Owner follow-up (chat, no new item): the fabrication row is not a \"Fabrication:\" + dropdown mix — it is ONE plain Label with the stage token only, \"\" until a board is loaded (seeded default ≠ loaded), the stage token and nothing else after. Landed as the next commit on main after 647717d: _fabrication_stage_label + _board_loaded (set on load_board_from_yaml and project restore), refreshed from data_changed; picker + commit handler deleted, stage is MCP-only. test_via_edit_and_fab_stage §11 → bare-readout test, test_pcb_panel_layout §7 asserts FabricationStageLabel and no FabricationStageOption; counts unchanged (81 / 148); authored, not run.","created_at":"2026-08-29T03:59:35"}
{"_type":"comment","id":184,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Owner re-HITL FAIL on 4be5ba6: sidebar tools in one long column, two orphan '---' at the foot. Root cause: the sidebar never owned a width — RightSidebar has no horizontal expand, so width == widest child min, which was the deleted Properties rows (60 px key + picker); without them the column fell to its 120 px floor. Fix (next commit on main): panel_layout.sidebar_width_px (wide 240 / medium+narrow 184) applied in _apply_layout_mode and at build. Dividers: DockSeparator visible only while the pane is in the sidebar (wide); the divider above the fabrication read-out removed. test_pcb_panel_layout 148→153, authored not run. NOTE: the single-column symptom is not fully explained by 120 px (24 px icons ≈ 36 px buttons → 3 per row); if the owner still sees one per row after this, a screenshot is needed — I could not measure headless with Minerva running (autoload/MCP port collision).","created_at":"2026-08-29T04:08:59"}
{"_type":"comment","id":185,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Re-HITL on 1de9073 still one column, now with empty space to the RIGHT of the buttons — that detail located the real cause: RightSidebarContent (the VBox inside RightSidebarScroll) had no SIZE_EXPAND_FILL, and Godot's ScrollContainer only stretches a child to its width when the child carries EXPAND; otherwise it sits at its minimum width. The Properties rows used to force that minimum ≥ the sidebar width; with them gone the VBox was one button wide and every FlowContainer wrapped one-per-line. Fix a5a95fc: one flag. The per-mode width (1de9073) stays and is correct; its 'tool flows stopped wrapping' rationale was over-claimed and is trimmed. Lesson recorded: a layout suite would have caught this — the 'three tools on one row' check was authored but not run.","created_at":"2026-08-29T04:14:50"}
{"_type":"comment","id":186,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Re-HITL on a5a95fc: wrapping works (\"better!\") but four-wide is too much in narrow layouts — owner wants responsive: 2 at min, 4+ when there is X room. Next commit on main: panel_layout.sidebar_width_px(panel_width) = clamp(0.20 × width, 88, 244) — 480→96 (2), 600→120 (3), 900→180 (4), 1220+→244 (6) — applied on every resize in _on_panel_resized and in _apply_layout_mode/_build_sidebar. Layout suite 153→154, pinned to the function; authored, not run. Knobs if the feel is off: SIDEBAR_SHARE / SIDEBAR_MIN_PX / SIDEBAR_MAX_PX.","created_at":"2026-08-29T04:19:02"}
{"_type":"comment","id":187,"item_id":"01a04b9c90647c8fbe505e37115a5187","author":"agent","text":"Re-HITL: hover cards accepted as done (U1S mystery = the part is LOCKED; get_component_at skips locked parts by design — reads-vs-drag split filed separately if wanted). New finding: wide mode, dock pane in sidebar — annotation list < 1 row tall over a blank column. Root cause = vertical twin of a5a95fc: RightSidebarContent had no size_flags_vertical EXPAND, so the ScrollContainer sized it to minimum height and AnnotationDockParent's expand-fill had no slack; the Properties rows used to hide the gap. AnnotationDockPane RIGHT mode already resets its minimum (_RIGHT_EXPANDED_MIN, list floor MIN_LIST_HEIGHT, EXPAND_FILL), so the plugin flag alone fixes it — next commit on main. Layout suite 154→156, authored not run.","created_at":"2026-08-29T04:42:43"}
{"_type":"comment","id":188,"item_id":"01a04c1a3ff17edbb2a145a05f512be0","author":"agent","text":"Linux resume 2026-08-29 06:1x–06:4x PT (Minerva down): (1) the seven named suites — 6/7 green first run; test_pcb_hover_card 109/1 → §7 hovered the pour's CENTRE, but a copper pour is picked only near its outline by design (keepouts by interior) → fixture moved to the top edge, 110/110 (434c3fc). (2) Minerva hermetic tier: two reds were a stale local class cache (UiScaleSync; hint godot/headless-tests-stale-class-cache-after-pull); after --import, test_ui_scale_sync 1/4 — the rig ran inside SceneTree._initialize before the root is in the tree, product guard correct → await one frame, 5/5; hermetic 12/12; --pcb-guard 13/13 + 6/6. Pushed to development (also the CI functional-tests job's only failure). (3) Deferred full suite for 864a99c..eebd655: pytest 2868/0; GD 81 suites, one red = test_pcb_width_prefs 33 vs pin 34 — 647717d removed the trace-width property row so a guarded check stopped executing; replaced with an unconditional \"row is gone\" check, 34/34 (afb9135). Full-suite baseline now 864a99c..afb9135.","created_at":"2026-08-29T06:40:08"}
{"_type":"comment","id":229,"item_id":"01a05168fac57f7986c9b242cff790c6","author":"agent","text":"Reproduces on pcb 0.6.0 (HITL 2026-09-02): minerva_pcb_load_board path=smart_remote_v2_board.yaml → board_health.indeterminate [{net: GND, reason: zone_copper, detail: \"canonical board schema requires an integer version 1 or 2 (present)\"}], complete:null; the deserialize reply carries \"version\":2.0 (float over JSON) and board_check one call later is clean. Not re-filed.","created_at":"2026-09-02T15:06:26"}
{"_type":"comment","id":189,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"Dispatch approved 2026-08-30. Bases: Minerva development a1cb6455; minerva-plugins main 6ac38fd. Planning finding that added T0: Note.Type.PLUGIN_DATA is wrapped by no provider (all wrap_memory handle IMAGE/TEXT only; 019df4ebf896 backlog; invoke_render_for_llm has no callers) — adopting the hooks in pcb without a host fix would blind chat on every provider. Order T0 (minerva 019df4ebf896 step-2 fallback in NotesContainer.to_prompt) → T1 (minerva 019df4f5426076 ChatGPT image parts) → T2 (plugins 01a05189fb84 pcb hooks). Owner rulings: image-first, caption = alt text (no DRC/worker at note time), full board dict payload. Minerva is DOWN for the cycle.","created_at":"2026-08-30T07:25:59"}
{"_type":"comment","id":190,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"T0 landed: Minerva development 76d811a (NotesContainer.wrap_notes static seam; PLUGIN_DATA → text stand-in (alt) + image stand-in (preview), stand-ins freed after wrap; test src/test/test_notes_to_prompt_plugin_data.gd, stub provider records handed sequence; authored not run). Audit: 1 commit, 2 files, base clean. Implementer findings (file-don't-fix): (1) to_prompt reads SingletonObject containers, never self — hermetic test had to target wrap_notes; cleanup candidate; (2) PluginProvider + HumanProvider wrap an IMAGE note as its caption, so a plugin_data note yields alt text twice there (pre-existing); (3) ClaudeCodeProvider + OpenAIImageProvider have no IMAGE branch — preview degrades to '' as for any image note; (4) empty-string wrap results are still appended (pre-existing); (5) new test has no .gd.uid yet — commit it after the scoped run generates it. T1 dispatched on base 76d811a.","created_at":"2026-08-30T07:31:46"}
{"_type":"comment","id":191,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"T1 landed: Minerva development 5e11216a (ChatGPTProvider.Format collects Image notes as standard image_url blocks on user turns only; _convert_content_types → {\"type\":\"input_image\",\"image_url\":\"data:image/png;base64,…\"} — bare string; _png_data_url helper; test src/test/test_chatgpt_image_notes.gd, oracle = decoded base64 equals source PNG bytes + pixel data). API fact VERIFIED by the implementer against developers.openai.com images-vision guide: Responses API input_image takes image_url as a bare string, NOT the Chat-Completions nested {url} the repo's OpenAI provider uses — the brief's fallback would have shipped the wrong shape. Audit: 1 commit, 2 files. Static gates: none run (no live LSP, Godot forbidden) — owed at the scoped run (Minerva is down, so godot --path is safe there). Findings filed-not-fixed: (1) estimate_tokens_from_prompt counts only *_text types but receives Format() output typed 'text' → ChatGPT EstimatedTokenCost always 0 (pre-existing); (2) no image-token estimator for ChatGPT; (3) Format ignores ChatHistoryItem.Images (CapabilityBroker mirrors them into InjectedNotes); (4) data-URL construction duplicated across 5 providers. T2 dispatched on plugins base 6ac38fd.","created_at":"2026-08-30T07:37:26"}
{"_type":"comment","id":192,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"T2 landed: plugins main 7bd1a11 (new pcb/ui/pcb_note.gd: build_note/restore_board/caption/capture_preview; PCBPanel.gd wiring only — two hooks, restore inside _restoring gate + _refresh_board_ui + _zoom_to_fit_deferred; pcb_canvas.capture_to_image split into capture_to_image_now because invoke_create_note is synchronous; payload = to_saved_board_dict (footprint_resolved stripped); test tests/gd/test_pcb_note_hooks.gd assertions=23, oracle = _whole_board_token over source vs fresh restored PCBData + preview aspect/size + exact caption string + refusals). Static: gd-syntax-check passed 4 files. Audit: 1 commit, 5 files. Filed-not-fixed: restore does not adopt source_path (no annotations/sidecar home for an Edit-from-note board); annotations/route hints not in the note; Minerva _build_note_from_plugin_payload discards the whole plugin_data shape when no Image (board payload lost for a cosmetic reason). Batch cold Fable review dispatched over Minerva a1cb6455..5e11216a + plugins 6ac38fd..7bd1a11.","created_at":"2026-08-30T07:55:41"}
{"_type":"comment","id":193,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"Fable batch review: must_fix — (1) T2's capture split forced the off-screen draw BEFORE the copied canvas processed its queued redraw (queue_redraw is MessageQueue-deferred; force_draw does not flush it) → blank preview AND a regression of minerva_pcb_get_image; (2) restore skipped _adopt_worker_anchors; (3) pcb_note comment overclaimed the host backfill; (4) stand-in notes duplicate the preview per send (noted); (5) redundant §1 token check. FOLDS: plugins b63770d (pcb_canvas.gd reverted byte-for-byte; build_note/capture_preview coroutines over the awaiting capture_to_image; PCBPanel hook awaits; restore adopts anchors; test stub → capture_to_image, redundant check dropped, pin 22) + Minerva ec04aa53 (PluginScenePanelHost.invoke_create_note `return await`s the hook; both Editor call sites await; new test test_plugin_host_create_note_await.gd: sync/coroutine/hookless). Re-review requested.","created_at":"2026-08-30T08:02:56"}
{"_type":"comment","id":194,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"Fable re-review of folds: all 5 resolved, no new defects, approve_with_notes (old-host/new-plugin coupling degrades to the screenshot fallback, no crash; _update_note already contained awaits pre-fold). Codex batch review running over Minerva a1cb6455..ec04aa53 + plugins 6ac38fd..b63770d (scratchpad/tc10_diff.patch, 1221 lines). SCOPED EXECUTION SET (named before running): Minerva — validating: test_notes_to_prompt_plugin_data, test_chatgpt_image_notes, test_plugin_host_create_note_await; regressions in touched modules/direct callers: test_plugin_data_persistence, test_presentation_panel_note_hooks, test_plugin_chat_providers. pcb — validating: test_pcb_note_hooks; regressions (consumers of capture_to_image / get_image / PCBPanel load-restore path): test_fab_preview_legibility, test_pcb_single_trace_tool, test_pcb_panel_tools_migration, test_pcb_panel_tools, test_pcb_workflow_kinds, test_view_state. Runtime bundles 0.5.3/0.5.4/0.5.5 parked for the pcb run; no Go change so no rebuild.","created_at":"2026-08-30T08:04:16"}
{"_type":"comment","id":195,"item_id":"01a0518a0c6c733db1907cc48910f460","author":"agent","text":"Codex batch review: must_fix — (1) _update_note yields but the Create Note button emitted UpdateUnsavedTabIcon before the refresh; (2) coroutine hook vs older Minerva host (payload lost to the screenshot fallback) — wants an enforced minimum host version; (3) narrative comments in pcb_note.gd/test. Dispositions: (1) fixed, Minerva 21f4d3a0 (await before emit). (2) ACCEPTED AS DEPLOYMENT CONSTRAINT — host_api_version is parsed (PluginDefinition.gd:719) but never compared, no enforcement point exists; gate filed as minerva work item 01a051b553 (bump contract to 2 once enforced). Constraint: the Minerva build carrying ec04aa53 (host awaits the create-note hook) must be installed before/with the pcb release carrying 7bd1a11; an older host degrades to today's screenshot note, no crash. (3) pcb_note.gd header trimmed (plugins 64a7073); test header kept by repo convention. Codex re-check running on the two folds.","created_at":"2026-08-30T08:07:51"}
